        <h3>🛠️ DIY Water Heater Strapping Guide & Reference</h3>
        <p>Installing seismic straps is a fast, low-cost DIY project that satisfies state code and keeps mortgage appraisers happy.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="background-color: var(--dynamic-bg-highlight); border: 1px solid var(--premier-beige); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
        <h4 style="margin-top:0; color: var(--premier-charcoal); font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 800;">4-Step DIY Installation Checklist:</h4>
        <ol style="margin-left: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--premier-charcoal);">
          <li><strong>Locate Wall Studs:</strong> Use a stud finder to locate framing studs on both sides of the tank. (If studs are misaligned, screw a horizontal 2x4 cross-brace into the studs first).</li>
          <li><strong>Position Upper & Lower Straps:</strong> Measure the top third and bottom third of the tank height. Keep the lower strap at least 4 inches above the lower gas/electric controls.</li>
          <li><strong>Anchor Lag Screws:</strong> Fasten heavy-duty metal belt straps into the wall studs using 1/4" x 3" lag screws with washers.</li>
          <li><strong>Tighten Tension Belts:</strong> Wrap belts around the front of the tank and tighten the cinch bolts until the tank is firmly immobilized against the wall.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

